+# Staff club/person route inspection
+
+Selected task: `001 Inspect current Staff club/person routes and forms, especially any club-scoped create-person/add-member path and /admin/clubs/:club_id/people/:person_id/edit`.
+
+## Current Staff routes
+
+`MembaWeb.Router` mounts the Staff club/person surface under the `/admin` scope with the `:staff_browser` pipeline:
+
+- `GET /admin/clubs` -> `MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Index`
+- `GET /admin/clubs/:club_id` -> `MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Show`
+- `GET /admin/clubs/:club_id/people/new` -> `MembaWeb.Admin.PeopleLive.New`
+- `GET /admin/clubs/:club_id/people/:person_id/edit` -> `MembaWeb.Admin.PeopleLive.Edit`
+
+There is currently no Staff invitation route under `/admin/clubs/:club_id/...`.
+
+## Current club-scoped creation/member paths
+
+`MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Show` is the current club detail page and exposes two separate Staff workflows:
+
+- A `New person` link (`#new-person-link`) to `/admin/clubs/:club_id/people/new`.
+- An `Add a member` form (`#add-member-form`) that submits the `add_member` LiveView event with only `membership[person_id]`.
+
+The `add_member` event generates a membership id, adds the current `club_id`, and calls `Membership.add_member(..., consistency: :strong)`. This creates an active club membership immediately for an existing projected person.
+
+`MembaWeb.Admin.PeopleLive.New` is the club-scoped person creation page. Its form (`#person-form`, aria-label `Create person`) collects:
+
+- name;
+- one primary email address;
+- optional alternate email addresses.
+
+Submitting `create_person` calls `Membership.create_person(..., consistency: :strong)` and navigates back to `/admin/clubs/:club_id`. It does not create membership by itself, but in combination with the club detail page's `Add a member` form it is the current Staff bypass for creating an active member from Staff-entered name/email.
+
+## Existing person edit route
+
+`MembaWeb.Admin.PeopleLive.Edit` backs `/admin/clubs/:club_id/people/:person_id/edit`.
+
+The route:
+
+- preserves club context and returns to `/admin/clubs/:club_id` after save/cancel;
+- displays the existing person name read-only;
+- lets Staff replace the person's primary/alternate email address set with `Membership.replace_person_email_addresses(..., consistency: :strong)`;
+- does not manage active memberships directly.
+
+The iteration plan says this route should remain available where needed for existing people.
+
+## Test and acceptance references to update later
+
+Current Phoenix tests assert the existing routes/selectors:
+
+- `web/test/memba_web/live/admin/clubs_live/show_test.exs`
+- `web/test/memba_web/live/admin_people_live_test.exs`
+- `web/test/memba_web/live/browser_acceptance_harness_test.exs`
+
+Current acceptance helper plumbing also drives direct person creation and add-member flows:
+
+- `acceptance-tests/features/support/member_message.js`
+- `acceptance-tests/features/support/server_commands.js`
+
+Later tasks that add invitations and decommission direct Staff member creation will need to update these tests/helpers intentionally rather than deleting the existing person edit coverage.
